eration.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. So decision quality good, attention good, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Concern for others is positive for crew cooperation. Mixed.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration, adaptability to unexpected. Concerns: moody, loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Likely candidate B has strong stress resilience, conscientiousness, technical (computer), but communication tone issues. Candidate C has decision speed, attention, but communication difficulty and egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Candidate A has anticipation, leadership, but unfriendly and unhealthy. Candidate D has responsibility, problem solving, but moody and loner.\n\nWhich is strongest overall? Probably Candidate B: reliability (conscientious), stress resilience, technical competence (computer), good weather assessment (operational). Communication concerns but can be mitigated. Compared to others, B seems balanced.\n\nThus I will recommend Candidate B.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion: none, but we can say \"Given the facts we have so far\". Provide evidence: conscientious, handles stress, good weather assessment, computer skills. Mention concerns: pretentious, tone, but overall still best.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE with that argument.\n\nMETADATA_JSON vote: Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
